Package: estrec
Type: Package
Title: Write Estimation Results as 'estimation' Records
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Ted", "Matherly", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "jemather@gmail.com")
Description: Writes fitted models as records in the 'estimation' format, a JSON
    file for one statistical estimation run: what was estimated, what came out,
    and how and where it ran. Version 0.1 writes 'fixest' fits: 'feols' (OLS and IV)
    and 'feglm'/'fepois' (GLMs), including multiple estimations, 'split' and
    'subset'; adds hypothesis tests
    and linear combinations to records, and writes sets of records as collections
    (a paper's results, a session or a replication).
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/estimation-format/estimation
BugReports: https://github.com/estimation-format/estimation/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: jsonlite, stats, utils
Suggests: broom, fixest (>= 0.12), generics, marginaleffects, modelsummary, openssl
Encoding: UTF-8
